 ZFILER Notes - 3/6 

      -- fixed buеееееееее under Z3PLUS.
      -- Path file conflicts are no longer reported under ZSDOS (this produced
      problems  when  users  triеееееееееremoved code which attempted to use the ZCPR Environment to determine
      how many lines of text to  display with  the V commеееееееееup Copy error messages are now sustained until the 
      user strikes a key, rather than disappearing immediately.
      -- Pеееееееееnow  hard-coded to 22,  so ZFILER  should  work on any 
      terminal with 24 or more screen rows.
      -- fixed  small  bugеееееееееnow  an "escape char" for script prompts,  and can 
      be used to include the $, ^, and ' characters in prompts.   Examples:еееееееееto file again), for use
      with terminal  definitions (TCAPs) which  define  control- J as an arrow
      key.
      -- idеееееееее   $"Type $"//$" for help: "        Type "//" for help:
      -- Move and  Group Move  now use the  option menu selections whenеееееееееe  date stamps with
      ring, requiring major rewrite).   It would be relatively simple to allow
      the Login and startupеееееееее of the
      tagged names.
      -- made the escape character and  the characters  to  quote with it when 
      writing a gеееееееее    -- $* script parameter was added to clear the screen during, and rebuild
      it after  a script prompt.   Usage is $"$*..еееееееее",  and quoted
      characters are currently "$", "|", and "<", as required by ZEX vs 5.
      -- it is now  possible to answеееееееее only characters
      which are quoted  when  ZFILER  builds  the  ZFILER.ZEX  file.   If they 
      appear in a  ZFILER.CMDеееееееее    directory.   Previously this  logged  in  all files  at user zero of the 
      current drive.   The Login  command  now  aеееееееееs
      is' to the ZEX file.   This  means  that  you cannot  use ZEX directives
      such as $1, |crlf|, etc., dynamically.еееееееееly reset
      when a command key is received.  This should allow Bridger Mitchell's AT
      command scheduler  RSX to  interеееееееее     -- Copy and Move commands now work properly with Z3PLUS, and the current
      12-hour time shows at the top of the screenеееееееееg which prevented  any Group commands from operating when the
      configuration byte MACFLAG was patched to false.
      -- еееееееееed  to  backup  directories  along  the path).  
      ZSDOS public conflicts are still reported.
      -- Group Move and  Groеееееееееand, as this was only 
      partially implemented, resulting in difficulty on terminals with over 24
      rows.  Text lines еееееееееrompts in scripts may now contain control chars as  "^x"  where x is 
      any char from @ to z.
      -- The dollar sign is еееееееее   which  caused  "Public  File  Error"  message  to 
      disappear.
